A continuous random variable has $f(x) = \dfrac{3x^{2}}{117}$ on $[2,5]$, and $0$ elsewhere.
Find $P(2 \le X \le 3)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.8cm, y=3.2cm]
\fill[gray!35, domain=2:3, variable=\x] (2,0) -- plot ({\x},{0.02564*\x*\x}) -- (3,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.8,0) -- (6.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.16) -- (0,0.86) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-0.7,0) -- (2,0);
\draw[thick, domain=2:5, smooth, samples=100, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.02564*\x*\x});
\draw (2,0) -- (2,0.1026);
\draw[thick] (5,0) -- (6.4,0);
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2$};
\node[below] at (3,0) {$3$};
\node[below] at (5,0) {$5$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A continuous random variable has $f(x) = \dfrac{x}{50}$ on $[0,10]$, and $0$ elsewhere.
Find $P(X \ge 7)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.46cm, y=10cm]
\fill[gray!35] (7,0) -- (7,0.14) -- (10,0.2) -- (10,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1,0) -- (12.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.05) -- (0,0.27) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-0.9,0) -- (0,0);
\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (10,0.2);
\draw[thick] (10,0) -- (12.2,0);
\node[below] at (7,0) {$7$};
\node[below] at (10,0) {$10$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A continuous random variable has $f(x) = \dfrac{x^{2}}{9}$ on $[0,3]$, and $0$ elsewhere.
Find $P(1 \le X \le 2)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.3cm, y=2.2cm]
\fill[gray!35, domain=1:2, variable=\x] (1,0) -- plot ({\x},{0.11111*\x*\x}) -- (2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.5,0) -- (4.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.22) -- (0,1.35) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-0.4,0) -- (0,0);
\draw[thick, domain=0:3, smooth, samples=100, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.11111*\x*\x});
\draw[thick] (3,0) -- (4,0);
\node[below] at (1,0) {$1$};
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2$};
\node[below] at (3,0) {$3$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
